---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="DIY Guides & Tutorials | CalcForDIY"
  description="Read our step-by-step guides and tutorials for home improvement, landscaping, and DIY projects."
>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    <a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-600">Home</a>
    <span>/</span>
    <span>Guides</span>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">DIY Guides & Tutorials</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-600 text-lg">Step-by-step instructions to help you plan your materials perfectly.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
    <a href="/guides/how-much-mulch-for-garden-beds" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Much Mulch Do I Need for Garden Beds?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn exactly how to calculate the amount of mulch you need for your garden beds, including measuring and depth recommendations.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/soil-4x8-raised-bed" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Much Soil to Fill a 4x8 Raised Bed?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">A practical breakdown of exactly how many bags or cubic yards you need to fill the most popular raised bed size, based on different depths.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-many-bags-of-grout-for-tile-shower" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Bags of Grout for a Tile Shower?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn how tile size and joint width affect your coverage, and calculate exactly how much material you need.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-many-studs-for-a-wall" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Studs Do I Need for a Wall?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn exactly how to calculate the number of studs needed for a wall, including the math for corners, doors, windows, and standard waste factors.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-much-concrete-for-fence-posts" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Much Concrete Do I Need for Fence Posts?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn the exact math formula to calculate how many bags of concrete you need for fence posts, including standard post hole sizes and frost line depths.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/laminate-flooring-waste-factor" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">What Waste Factor Should I Use for Laminate Flooring?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn exactly what waste factor percentage you need when buying laminate flooring, depending on your room shape, layout pattern, and DIY skill level.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-many-recessed-lights-for-a-2-car-garage" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Recessed Lights Do I Need for a 2-Car Garage?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Step-by-step guide on calculating target lumens, grid layout spacing, ceiling height considerations, and color temperature.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-much-tile-do-i-need-for-a-shower" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Much Tile Do I Need for a Shower?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Calculate wall area, floor pan mosaics, curb, and niche square footage, plus waste factor percentages for straight vs diagonal layouts.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-many-boxes-of-hardwood-flooring" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Boxes of Hardwood Flooring Do I Need?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn how to convert room square footage into exact carton counts, handling box coverage variations and waste factors.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-many-roofing-squares" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Squares of Shingles for a 2,000 Sq Ft Roof?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn how to calculate roofing squares, pitch multipliers, bundle counts (3 bundles = 1 square), starter strips, and waste factors.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-many-fence-pickets" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Fence Pickets Do I Need for 100 Feet?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn how to calculate fence pickets for a 100-foot fence, accounting for picket widths, gap spacing, post deductions, and waste buffers.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-much-attic-insulation" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Much Blown-In Insulation Do I Need for My Attic?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Calculate bags of blown fiberglass/cellulose to hit R-38, R-49, or R-60 energy code depth, machine rental hours, and soffit baffles.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/conduit-size-for-3-wires" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">What Size Conduit Do I Need for 3 Wires?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn what size EMT or PVC conduit you need for 3 THHN copper wires (14 AWG to 2 AWG) based on the NEC 40% maximum conduit fill rule.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-far-can-2x8-deck-joist-span" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Far Can a 2x8 Deck Joist Span?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn maximum allowable spans for 2x8 deck joists (SYP, Cedar, Doug Fir) at 12", 16", and 24" o.c. spacing per IRC Table R507.5.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/what-gauge-wire-for-50-amp-ev-charger" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">What Gauge Wire for a 50-Amp EV Charger?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Detailed NEC wire sizing guide comparing 6/3 NM-B Romex vs 6 AWG THHN in conduit for 50A Level 2 chargers.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-many-bags-of-concrete-for-4x4-post" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Bags of Concrete for a 4x4 Fence Post?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Bag lookup table for 50 lb Fast-Setting vs 80 lb standard concrete bags based on hole diameter and frost line depth.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-to-calculate-soffit-ventilation" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How to Calculate Soffit &amp; Attic Ventilation (1:300 Rule)</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Calculate required Net Free Vent Area (NFVA in sq in) and balanced 50/50 soffit intake and ridge exhaust per IRC R806.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-much-tile-for-standard-shower" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Much Tile Do I Need for a Standard Shower?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Complete square footage takeoff for 36x36, 36x48, and 36x60 showers, mosaic pan floors, niches, and TCNA waste factors.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/ice-and-water-shield-requirements" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">Ice &amp; Water Shield Code Requirements &amp; Sizing</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn IRC Section R905.1.2 ice barrier codes, required 24" inside heated wall calculations, and 200 sq ft roll quantities.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-to-cut-crown-molding" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How to Measure &amp; Cut Crown Molding (Miter &amp; Bevel Chart)</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Compound miter saw angles (31.62° miter / 33.86° bevel) for 90° corners, 135° bay windows, and 4-direction cut guide.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-many-bags-of-concrete-for-sonotube" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Bags of Concrete for a Sonotube (8, 10, 12, 16 In)?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Exact bag count lookup table (60 lb and 80 lb Quikrete) for Sonotube pier footings based on diameter and frost depth.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-deep-should-a-gravel-driveway-be" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Deep Should a Gravel Driveway Be? (3-Layer Guide)</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Complete aggregate layer guide: 4-6" of #3 ballast stone, 3" of #57 stone, 2" crusher run top coat, and geotextile fabric.</p>
    </a>
      <a href="/guides/how-many-cinder-blocks-for-retaining-wall" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Cinder Blocks for a Retaining Wall?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Step-by-step formulas and sizing charts for calculating 8x8x16 CMU blocks, Type S mortar bags, core grout fill, and footing rebar.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-much-stain-do-i-need-for-a-deck" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Much Stain Do I Need for a Deck?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Learn the 2.5x railing multiplier, wood porosity coverage rates, and exact gallon calculations for single vs. double coat staining.</p>
    </a>
      <a href="/guides/how-many-boxes-of-vinyl-plank-flooring" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How Many Boxes of Vinyl Plank Flooring Do I Need?</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">Room measurement formulas, carton square footage conversions, and straight vs. herringbone pattern waste factors.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/guides/how-to-calculate-voltage-drop-for-wire-runs" class="block bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:border-blue-500 hover:shadow-md transition-all">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">How to Calculate Voltage Drop for Long Wire Runs</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm">The official NEC Ohm's law formula and circular mil charts for sizing wire to subpanels, workshops, and EV chargers.</p>
    </a>
  </div>

</Layout>
